title: "Animal call tests often fire on null data, but most effects still hold"
abstract: "Across nine pre-registered re-tests of headline animal-communication claims, 8 of 10 published-style procedures reported an effect in at least 30% of worlds that had none. With calibrated tests, five claims held in full or in part, one did not, and three remain undecided. Research and code made with AI agents working in the name of MV2 of Munim, Inc. Code licensed Apache-2.0; text and data CC BY 4.0 unless a file says otherwise."
